e 'Contact Us' page, create and embed a new form using 'Contact Form 7' to allow users to send messages.\\\\n31. On the 'Public Documents' page, create links to upload and display non-sensitive files like Bylaws and Architectural Guidelines.\\\\n32. For the 'News and Updates' section, use the built-in 'Posts' feature of WordPress. Instruct the user on how to create a new post, assign it a category (e.g., 'Announcements'), and publish it.\\\\n\\\\n**Phase 9: Final Review**\\\\n33. Log out of WordPress and view the website as a public user to ensure all public pages are visible and restricted pages are not.\\\\n34. Register a test user account through the MemberPress registration page.\\\\n35. Log in as the test user and verify that all resident-only pages are now accessible.\\\\n36. Provide the user with the final WordPress login credentials.\\\"\\n}\\n###2025-07-17T22:10:30.500Z###\"}]},\"finishReason\":\"stop\",\"custom\":{}}],\"custom\":{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"parts\":[{\"text\":\"I have received the draft Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) from Director Yularen. This resolves order `ORDER-YULAREN-002`. My previous `RUNAWAY_CALL_WARNING` must have been a system glitch that has since cleared.\\n\\nThe DEP is comprehensive and detailed, providing a clear, step-by-step guide for a non-technical user. It successfully integrates the technology stack with the required site structure.\\n\\nThis DEP marks the completion of the Planning phase. The next and final action in this phase is to request a shift to the Execution phase. I will issue a `PHASE` system call, providing the justification and the complete DEP string as formulated by Director Yularen. Upon approval by the user, we will begin executing this plan one directive at a time.\\n\\n###2025-07-17T22:10:30.500Z###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: PHASE\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"My team has successfully completed the planning process. We have analyzed the user's requirements for an HOA website, select